<descriptor-repository version="1.0">

    <!-- The OJB database table defined by this file will contain all of the attribute data for the business object class described.
         
         A table should exist for every Cemi{EXTRACTNAME}File{TABNAME}TabRowBo required by the data extraction spreadsheet file.
         Meaning: 
            Award Schedule data extract file would need one table for its business object:
                CemiAwardScheduleFileAwardScheduleTabRowBo
            while the Supplier data extract file would require six tables for its business objects (not in the template format yet)
                CemiSupplierFileSupplierRowBo:
                CemiSupplierFileAddressesRowBo
                CemiSupplierFileEmailsRowBo
                CemiSupplierFilePhonesRowBo
                CemiSupplierFileBankAccountsRowBo
                CemiSupplierFileChildrenRowBo
         
         Table names should be in the format of CU_CEMI_EXTR_XXX_XXX_TAB_YYY_YYY_T where 
            XXX_XXX represents the data extract name
            YYY_YYY represents a tab name in the mapping template spreadsheet of the extract file
         
         Class descriptor items should set the "schema" attribute to "CEMI" so that OJB knows to access the table
         on the CEMI schema side.

         Table field descriptor items should follow this pattern:
            First two descriptors should represent the standard CemiIndexedBusinessObjectBase attributes defined as the table's composite primary key:
                EXTR_FILE_RUNDATE VARCHAR2(20) NOT NULL from the SQL script would have values
                    name="jobRunDateString"
                    column="EXTR_FILE_RUNDATE"
                    jdbc-type="VARCHAR"
                    primarykey="true"
                    index="true"
                JOB_RUN_ROW_INDEX NUMBER(14,0) NOT NULL from the SQL script would have values:
                    name="jobRunRowIndex"
                    column="JOB_RUN_ROW_INDEX"
                    jdbc-type="BIGINT"
                    primarykey="true"
                    index="true
                    
            The remaining field-descriptors should exist for each legacy object key attribute as well as 
            mapping template spreadsheet field attribute defined in Cemi{EXTRACTNAME}File{TABNAME}TabRowBo where:
                name = attibute name
                column = define column name as either a standard KFS column name (for reference data) or have column name reflect attribute name
                jdbc-type = VARCHAR
                
            !!!!!VERY IMPORTANT!!!!!
                (a) For any data value that should be encrypted, ensure that the following IS present in that item's field-descriptor
                        conversion="org.kuali.kfs.core.framework.persistence.ojb.conversion.OjbKualiEncryptDecryptFieldConversion"
                (b) Add scrubbing SQL to nonprod-sql script in manual/kfs to scrub that particular field.
                    

         Create SQL script to build the physical database table CU_CEMI_EXTR_XXX_XXX_TAB_XXX_XXX_T
            (1) That SQL script should be created in folder kfs of repository nonprod-sql.
            (2) That SQL script should follow the file naming convention of
                cemi-AAA-EXTRACT-NAME-step-001-create-tables.sql
                where AAA is a numeric value representing that SQL extract in the overall SQL run order.
                Example:
                    cemi-001-suppliers-step-001-create-tables.sql
                    cemi-002-award-schedule-step-001-create-tables.sql
                            ...
                    cemi-005-order-from-step-001-create-tables.sql
    -->
